lv_event: take event-list memory off LVGL's heap

A display's event list churns continuously while anything is drawing -- every
label marked for a text refresh registers a callback and removes it on the next
layout pass. The pointer array reallocates, and TLSF may place the new buffer in
a pool the application has lent LVGL, where it cannot be recovered:
lv_mem_remove_pool requires the pool empty, and block_can_split needs 16 + size
while block_size_min is 12. The per-callback descriptors have the same problem,
living on LVGL's heap for as long as the callback is registered.

Both ends are routed to oxivgl_event_*. lv_array_init/push_back/resize/deinit
allocate through lv_realloc/lv_free internally, so this cannot be done by
swapping call sites -- event lists get their own array helpers, and lv_array.c
stays untouched because it is shared with lv_scale, the vector path ops and
lv_circle_buf.

--- a/src/misc/lv_event.c
+++ b/src/misc/lv_event.c
@@ -9,9 +9,30 @@
 #include "lv_event_private.h"
 #include "../core/lv_global.h"
 #include "../stdlib/lv_mem.h"
+#include "lv_array.h"
 #include "lv_assert.h"
+#include "../stdlib/lv_string.h"
 #include "lv_types.h"
 
+#include <stddef.h>
+
+/* Event-list memory does NOT come from LVGL's heap.
+ *
+ * A descriptor and the pointer array that holds it live for exactly as long as
+ * the callback is registered, which is arbitrary: `lv_label_mark_need_refr_text`
+ * registers one on the DISPLAY and removes it on the next layout pass, so any
+ * drawing churns these allocations continuously. A consumer that lends LVGL a
+ * pool for the duration of some operation therefore finds event memory in it,
+ * and cannot take the pool back -- `lv_tlsf_remove_pool` requires the pool
+ * empty, and the block cannot be trimmed away because `block_can_split` needs
+ * `16 + size` while `block_size_min` is 12.
+ *
+ * Routing is unconditional on purpose. A conditional route would leave the
+ * default build with the original defect and nothing to observe it. */
+extern void * oxivgl_event_malloc(size_t size);
+extern void * oxivgl_event_realloc(void * ptr, size_t size);
+extern void oxivgl_event_free(void * ptr);
+
 /*********************
  *      DEFINES
  *********************/
